LB1 #834 — Canonical pending_review lifecycle + orchestrator quota gate

Per user directive (no parallel paths), held AI runs reuse the existing
pending_review state and decide_task_approval contract instead of a new
held_for_review surface. Quota enforcement moves up from the AI adapter
into the orchestrator so every agent kind benefits.

Migration 20260425000000_lb1_lifecycle_quota.sql:
- Extends assert_task_transition (rebased on the L3 rollback matrix from
  20260421100000 so rolling_back / rollback_failed edges are preserved):
  adds running→pending_review and pending_review→{succeeded,failed}.
- Replaces decide_task_approval to detect post-execute holds via
  execution_result IS NOT NULL → terminal succeeded/failed.
- Drops release_held_ai_response RPC and the held_for_review /
  held_reason / released_by / released_at columns + index. Drops the
  v_ai_runs view first to free column dependencies, then recreates it
  deriving held fields from status / blocked_reason / completed_at.

Orchestrator-v2:
- New AgentQuotaGate dep + QUOTA_EXCEEDED code. Pre-execute Step 2b
  short-circuits to blocked BEFORE lock acquisition when the gate
  refuses; gate skipped when the task has no agent_id.
- Sensitive-output path now transitions running→pending_review (writing
  blocked_reason + execution_result) instead of marking succeeded with a
  parallel held flag. Returns finalStatus=blocked / errorCode=REVIEW_HOLD.
  Approval-requested event emitted by the DB trigger (no double-emit).

AI adapter: removed the Step-2 quota.peek call (orchestrator now owns
the gate); quota.consume() is still called in Step 5 for accounting.

Persistence (post-review fix): SupabaseTaskRepository now hydrates
agent_id, blocked_reason, approved_at, rejected_by — without this the
orchestrator's `task.agent_id` was always undefined in production and
the quota gate silently skipped every run.

Bootstrap: execution-loop wires a peek_agent_quota-backed gate.
Repo + UI: agents-repo derives held_for_review from status; admin runs
page replaces inline release/reject controls with a deep-link to
/admin/approvals so reviews flow through the canonical inbox.

Approvals UI deep-link (review fix):
- AdminApprovalsPage now reads `?taskId=<uuid>` from the URL and
  auto-opens the decision drawer, clearing the param on close.
- ApprovalDecisionDrawer renders an AI-metadata panel (purpose, verifier
  outcome, tools used, generated response) sourced from
  `execution_result` so reviewers can judge held AI runs without raw
  JSON spelunking.

Validation: tsc clean; full targeted suites green —
orchestrator-v2.test.ts 34/34 (3 new LB1 tests), ai-adapter.test.ts
10/10, AdminApprovalsPage.test.tsx 9/9. Migration not run against the
live DB in this session — applies on next supabase deploy.
